NumPy ziggurat constants and sampler
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Files:      src/numpyzig/ziggurat_constants.h
            src/zurand_engine.h, zig_normal_slow(), zig_normal_reject(),
              zig_normal_at() and the layer-0 tail of mcf_normal_edge()
              (derived from random_standard_normal() in
              numpy/random/src/distributions/distributions.c)
Copyright:  Copyright (c) 2005-2025, NumPy Developers. All rights reserved.
License:    BSD 3-clause
Full text:  src/numpyzig/LICENSE
Source:     https://github.com/numpy/numpy

Provides the lookup tables and layer layout for the ziggurat normal
sampler in rng_normal(). The header is trimmed to the normal-double tables
(ki_double, wi_double, fi_double, ziggurat_nor_r, ziggurat_nor_inv_r); the
float and exponential tables upstream also defines are removed, and what
is kept is otherwise unmodified. A comment at the top of the file records
the source, copyright and the trim.

The sampler follows random_standard_normal(): the same split of one 64-bit
word into layer index, sign and 52-bit magnitude, the same fast-path
accept test, the same wedge test against exp(-x^2 / 2), and Marsaglia's
tail with the same expressions. Modified: retry words come from
per-position Philox blocks so that each draw is a pure function of its
key and position, the sign is folded into a signed copy of the width
table, most wedge decisions are settled by the fixed-point brackets of
src/zigbounds.h, and exp() and log1p() are zurand's fdlibm port. These
derived portions remain under NumPy's BSD 3-clause license.


